Chrome Web Store installs and updates (the user's choice; docs/browser.md,
"Extensions"), on top of ungoogled-chromium: its installer comes back
(inox-patchset 0005 emptied it), extension update checks run while the
component updater stays off (block-requests.patch), extensions update from
the store's own server, and the store gets its own process again
(disable-webstore-urls.patch). Less goes to Google: no separate install,
update or uninstall event pings, no "managed computer" flag, checks once a
day. The checks themselves still carry what Chromium's update protocol
sends: the extensions' ids and versions, active-day counters and install
dates (docs/browser.md, "Extensions"). The store's addresses stay real
because files/hudhud/scripts/prepare-source.sh leaves the files in
files/hudhud/ungoogled/not-substituted.list out of the domain
substitution.

